WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.488
A man from the hunting party turned to Vinnie and the young boy.

2
00:00:04.489 --> 00:00:08.341
"Sequoia, we are leaving," he said.

3
00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:11.983
"Will they give us cattle?" asked Sequoia.

4
00:00:11.984 --> 00:00:15.510
The man nodded and turned his horse around.

5
00:00:15.511 --> 00:00:18.272
The boy followed.

6
00:00:18.273 --> 00:00:21.875
"What are you doing, Frank?" Vinnie asked.

7
00:00:21.876 --> 00:00:25.828
The cowboys were taking some of the cows from the herd.

8
00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:30.186
"We’re giving cattle to the Cherokee," replied Frank.

9
00:00:30.187 --> 00:00:32.250
"They are very hungry.

10
00:00:32.251 --> 00:00:34.946
These cattle will keep them alive.

11
00:00:34.947 --> 00:00:38.978
Plus, we must have peace between us."

12
00:00:38.979 --> 00:00:43.459
Vinnie watched the Cherokee ride off with the cattle.

13
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:47.821
"What if you didn’t give them anything?" Vinnie asked.

14
00:00:47.822 --> 00:00:50.959
Frank got back on his horse and said,

15
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.752
"They probably would have attacked."

16
00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.618
Vinnie shivered.

17
00:00:56.619 --> 00:01:00.481
Cookie got back onto the wagon beside Mandy.

18
00:01:00.482 --> 00:01:03.851
"Is everything okay?" she asked.

19
00:01:03.852 --> 00:01:07.659
"There’s nothing to worry about," said Cookie.

20
00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.692
The cowboys continued along the Chisholm Trail.

21
00:01:11.693 --> 00:01:16.001
They rode for hours, and Mandy was getting tired.

22
00:01:16.002 --> 00:01:20.661
"We’re at the end of the trail now," Cookie said to Mandy.

23
00:01:20.662 --> 00:01:22.842
He pointed ahead.

24
00:01:22.843 --> 00:01:27.218
Mandy could see some buildings and men on horses.

25
00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:30.967
"What is that place called?" she asked.

26
00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:34.831
"That’s Dodge City," Cookie answered.

27
00:01:34.832 --> 00:01:37.507
Frank rode up to the wagon.

28
00:01:37.508 --> 00:01:41.522
"Why don’t you take the kids to the hotel, Cookie?

29
00:01:41.523 --> 00:01:44.342
We’ll get the cattle to the market."

30
00:01:44.343 --> 00:01:50.449
Cookie urged the wagon’s horses forward, and Vinnie followed close behind.

31
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.106
"See you at the hotel!"

32
00:01:52.107 --> 00:01:57.366
called Frank as he led the cowboys in another

33
00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:01.364
direction. Cookie and the kids went to the center of

34
00:02:01.365 --> 00:02:07.160
town. Dodge City was muddy and noisy, and cowboys were

35
00:02:07.161 --> 00:02:10.091
everywhere. Their faces were different

36
00:02:10.092 --> 00:02:13.012
colors. They were dressed in different

37
00:02:13.013 --> 00:02:18.337
ways. But they were alike in one way—they all were dusty and

38
00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:23.505
dirty.The men laughed loudly and seemed to be having a good time.

39
00:02:23.506 --> 00:02:28.229
Cookie stopped his horses in front of a large wooden building.

40
00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.854
The entrance had swinging wooden doors.

41
00:02:31.855 --> 00:02:37.555
The children could hear a piano and lots of shouting.

42
00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:39.996
"What’s this place?"

43
00:02:39.997 --> 00:02:43.762
asked Vinnie, patting his horse’s neck.

44
00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:49.122
Suddenly, a man stumbled backward through the swinging doors.

45
00:02:49.123 --> 00:02:51.802
He landed in the muddy street.

46
00:02:51.803 --> 00:02:55.775
Another man came out shaking his fist.

47
00:02:55.776 --> 00:02:59.071
"This is the saloon," said Cookie.

48
00:02:59.072 --> 00:03:01.625
"Not a place for children."

49
00:03:01.626 --> 00:03:05.339
Cookie took them across the street to the hotel.

50
00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:12.423
Inside, families were eating at tables and people were playing cards.

51
00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:17.492
"Nellie?" Cookie called to a pretty young woman wearing an apron.

52
00:03:17.493 --> 00:03:21.804
"Howdy," she said in a friendly voice.

53
00:03:21.805 --> 00:03:25.720
"Glad to see you’re back from the trail safely."

54
00:03:25.721 --> 00:03:28.679
"Thanks, Nellie," said Cookie.

55
00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.417
He introduced the children.

56
00:03:31.418 --> 00:03:34.026
"Keep an eye on them for me.

57
00:03:34.027 --> 00:03:37.795
I’m going to the saloon for a little drink."

58
00:03:37.796 --> 00:03:43.878
"Hey, kids, we’re about to have a square dance in the back room," said Nellie.

59
00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:50.447
"Do you want to dance?"

